{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe supported public `rebar.mcp_server.build_server()` path emits `pydantic_settings.sources.utils.IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning` on its first FastMCP construction under the locked MCP 1.29.0 / pydantic-settings 2.15.0 dependency pair. Promoting the warning to an error aborts MCP startup.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nMCP v1 defines generic `mcp.server.fastmcp.server.Settings` before `FastMCP` while postponed annotations are enabled. Its `lifespan` field remains an unresolved `ForwardRef` and the upstream module never calls `Settings.model_rebuild()` after `FastMCP` is defined. Pydantic-settings 2.15 intentionally detects this unsafe incomplete field when settings sources inspect it. Direct upstream `FastMCP(\"direct\")` reproduces without rebar; the 2.14.2/2.15.0 A/B proves 2.15 exposed a pre-existing MCP defect. Upstream issue modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#3294 confirms the mechanism and endorses an after-import `Settings.model_rebuild()` workaround because MCP v1 is critical-fixes-only.\n\n## Repair Plan\n1. At rebar’s existing lazy MCP import boundary in `build_server()`, import the MCP v1 Settings model and invoke its public Pydantic `model_rebuild()` before either stdio or HTTP FastMCP construction. Keep the compatibility action inside the optional-dependency boundary; do not make MCP a core import.\n2. Do not suppress the warning, pin/downgrade dependencies, change MCP transport configuration, or migrate to MCP v2. This repair resolves the incomplete model metadata while preserving all settings values, lifecycle callbacks/contexts, tool registrations, and input/output schemas.\n3. Add a fresh-subprocess facade contract test. A subprocess is required because a successful first FastMCP construction auto-completes the process-global model and could mask the defect in an in-process suite. The subprocess promotes exactly `IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning` to an error, calls public `build_server()`, and asserts successful construction of the named `rebar` server.\n4. Verify the focused warning-as-error oracle, the complete MCP output-schema coverage module, stdio construction, real Streamable-HTTP initialize/lifespan behavior, lint, and typecheck.\n\n## Test Contract Card\n- authoritative_contract: pydantic-settings 2.15 defines incomplete FieldInfo as unsafe for settings-source inspection and prescribes `model_rebuild()`; rebar publishes `rebar-mcp`/`build_server()` over the supported MCP v1 range.\n- trigger_preconditions: a fresh Python interpreter, the supported MCP extra, and the exact warning category promoted to error before the first public server construction.\n- production_path: subprocess -> `rebar.mcp_server.build_server()` -> MCP `FastMCP.__init__` -> `Settings` sources.\n- test_tier: subprocess facade contract; an in-process unit is insufficient because first construction mutates global model completeness.\n- observable_postcondition: subprocess exits 0 and reports the constructed server name `rebar`; no warning suppression is permitted.\n- ci_gate: focused pytest node plus the repository `make test` gate.\n- negative_control: omitted as a genuinely single first-construction defect; existing normal stdio and real HTTP lifecycle tests are the behavior-preservation controls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The exact MCP v1 owning model and unresolved `lifespan` annotation remain documented in the ticket RCA with discriminating runtime evidence.\n- [ ] A fresh-process public `build_server()` call succeeds with `IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning` promoted to an error.\n- [ ] The repair completes the upstream Settings model rather than suppressing the warning or downgrading/pinning pydantic-settings.\n- [ ] MCP remains an optional lazy import and no dependency is added.\n- [ ] Existing stdio construction, Streamable-HTTP initialize/lifespan behavior, and the full MCP output-schema coverage module remain green.\n- [ ] Lint and typecheck pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_settings_completion.py`\n- `pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py`\n- `pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py::test_build_server_default_is_stdio_fastmcp tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py::test_http_transport_boots_and_serves_initialize`\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786917615953328001,"uuid":"f4f7d22d-765e-4f9e-b0f5-e2853e10b6fa"}